              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "Depending on what you are trying to do, **\"iCloud Control\"** can refer to a few different things. It most commonly refers to a third-party Mac utility, the official Windows integration app, or native settings on Apple devices. \n\n---\n\n### 1. \"iCloud Control\" for Mac (Third-Party Utility)\nIf you are on a Mac, **iCloud Control** is a popular, free, open-source utility designed to give you more power over how iCloud Drive syncs.\n* **What it does:** By default, macOS automatically decides which files are kept locally on your hard drive and which are stored only in the cloud. This tool adds a Finder menu that lets you manually force selective synchronization\u2014allowing you to easily download folders to your Mac or evict them to save disk space.\n* **How to get it:** You can download it directly from its GitHub repository (`Obbut/iCloud-Control`) or install it via Homebrew using the command:  \n  `brew install --cask icloud-control`\n\n*(Note: In newer versions of macOS, Apple has added native control to Finder. You can right-click any file or folder in iCloud Drive and select **\"Remove Download\"** to free up local space, or click the **cloud/download icon** to download it permanently.)*\n\n---\n\n### 2. \"iCloud Control Panel\" (iCloud for Windows)\nIf you are using a PC, **iCloud Control Panel** is the legacy name for **iCloud for Windows**, Apple\u2019s official software to bridge Apple services with Windows PCs.\n* **What it does:** It lets you access and manage your Apple data on a Windows computer. From this panel, you can control:\n  * **iCloud Photos:** View, upload, and download photos directly in Windows File Explorer or the Microsoft Photos app.\n  * **iCloud Drive:** Access your cloud files and documents in Windows File Explorer.\n  * **Passwords:** Sync and auto-fill your iCloud Keychain passwords in browsers like Chrome and Edge.\n  * **Mail, Contacts, and Calendars:** Sync your Apple data with Microsoft Outlook.\n  * **Bookmarks:** Sync your Safari bookmarks with Chrome, Firefox, or Edge.\n* **How to get it:** You can download the latest version for free from the **Microsoft Store** by searching for \"iCloud\". \n\n---\n\n### 3. Native iCloud Settings (Controlling iCloud on Apple Devices)\nIf you want to manage your iCloud storage, backups, and app syncing natively on your devices:\n\n* **On iPhone, iPad, or Apple Vision Pro:**\n  1. Open the **Settings** app.\n  2. Tap **your name** at the very top.\n  3. Tap **iCloud**. Here you can manage your storage, see which apps are backing up to the cloud, and upgrade your iCloud+ storage.\n* **On a Mac:**\n  1. Click the **Apple logo** (\uf8ff) in the top-left corner.\n  2. Select **System Settings**.\n  3. Click **your name** at the top of the sidebar.\n  4. Select **iCloud** to toggle syncing for specific apps, manage your storage, or set up features like Private Relay and Hide My Email.\n* **On any web browser:**\n  Go to **[iCloud.com](https://www.icloud.com)**, sign in with your Apple ID, and you can view, edit, or delete mail, photos, files, notes, and contacts from any computer.",
